### Order Saga Test Requests
### IntelliJ HTTP Client file
###
### Run infrastructure and services first.
### Full Docker:
### docker compose up --build -d
###
### Development mode:
### docker compose up -d order-db inventory-db payment-db kafka kafka-ui
### Then run order-service, inventory-service, and payment-service from IntelliJ.
###
### Kafka UI:
### http://localhost:8085
###
### Main API:
@orderBaseUrl = http://localhost:8081

### Known inventory seed data assumed by the project
### SKU 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111 has enough stock.
### SKU 11111111-1111-1111-2222-111111111111 has low stock, for example 2 units.
###
### Payment simulation rules assumed by FakePaymentAuthorizer:
### paymentMethodId starts with 11111111 -> authorized
### paymentMethodId starts with 22222222 -> business failure
### paymentMethodId starts with 33333333 -> technical failure, retry, then DLT


### 1. Happy path
### Expected final flow:
### POST /orders:
###      OrderCreated -> InventoryReserved -> PaymentRequested -> PaymentAuthorized -> order status = CONFIRMED
### Expected final order status: CONFIRMED
POST {{orderBaseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: aaaaaaaa-1111-2222-3333-aaaaaaaaaaaa

{
  "requestId": "10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "checkoutId": "20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "customerId": "30000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "paymentMethodId": "11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "currency": "DKK",
  "totalAmount": 50.00,
  "items": [
    {
      "skuId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
      "productName": "Demo Product A",
      "quantity": 2,
      "unitPrice": 25.00,
      "itemTotalPrice": 50.00
    }
  ]
}


### 2. Duplicate create order request
### Send exactly the same requestId as test 1.
### Expected :
### No new order / no new OrderCreated outbox event / response duplicate = true
POST {{orderBaseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
