### Manual Kafka tests
###
### These tests cannot be sent through order-service HTTP directly.
### Use Kafka UI at http://localhost:8085.
###
### A. Invalid OrderCreated message:
### Topic: order.created.v1
### Expected: inventory-service rejects message and sends it to order.created.v1.DLT
###
### Payload:
### {
###   "eventId": null,
###   "orderId": "bbbbbbbb-bbbb-bbbb-bbbb-bbbbbbbbbbbb",
###   "items": []
### }
###
### B. Invalid PaymentRequested message:
### Topic: payment.requested.v1
### Expected: payment-service rejects message and sends it to payment.requested.v1.DLT
###
### Payload:
### {
###   "eventId": null,
###   "orderId": "bbbbbbbb-bbbb-bbbb-bbbb-bbbbbbbbbbbb",
###   "amount": -1,
###   "currency": "DKK",
###   "paymentMethodId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111"
### }
###
### C. Invalid InventoryReleased message:
### Topic: inventory.released.v1
### Expected: order-service rejects message and sends it to inventory.released.v1.DLT
###
### Payload:
### {
###   "eventId": null,
###   "orderId": "bbbbbbbb-bbbb-bbbb-bbbb-bbbbbbbbbbbb"
### }


### Useful database checks
###
### orderdb:
### SELECT id, order_number, request_id, status, cancellation_reason, total_amount
### FROM orders
### ORDER BY created_at DESC;
###
### SELECT aggregate_type, aggregate_id, event_type, status, retry_count, last_error, payload
### FROM outbox_events
### ORDER BY created_at DESC;
###
### inventorydb:
### SELECT sku_id, available_quantity
### FROM inventory_items
### ORDER BY sku_id;
###
### SELECT order_id, sku_id, quantity, status, released_at
### FROM inventory_reservations
### ORDER BY created_at DESC;
###
### SELECT event_type, status, retry_count, last_error, payload
### FROM outbox_events
### ORDER BY created_at DESC;
###
### paymentdb:
### SELECT id, order_id, status, failure_reason, amount, currency
### FROM payments
### ORDER BY created_at DESC;
###
### SELECT event_type, status, retry_count, last_error, payload
### FROM outbox_events
### ORDER BY created_at DESC;
